# This is an EXAMPLE file, not an active configuration.
#
# GitHub Pages uses a file literally named "CNAME" (no extension) in the
# repository root to connect a custom domain to your Pages site.
#
# To use a custom domain:
#   1. Copy this file's content into a new file named exactly "CNAME"
#      (case-sensitive, no file extension) in the repository root.
#   2. Replace the placeholder below with your real domain.
#   3. Commit and push the "CNAME" file.
#   4. Configure DNS as described in README.md.
#
# PLACEHOLDER — replace with your real domain, then rename this file to CNAME:
www.example.com
